### Two things to know before editing these areas
- **Breadcrumbs must `strip_tags()` headline fields.** The MCS hero printed literal `<em>` tags in its breadcrumb because the headline is now accent-capable but the breadcrumb escaped it. `page-automated-system.php` had it right; copy that pattern.
- **The `#location_grand_rapids` / `#location_flat_rock` anchors are load-bearing** — `assets/css/legacy.css` targets them. They are now an explicit `anchor` field, *not* derived from the location name. Deriving them breaks the responsive rules silently.

### Removed dead fields
`mcs_hero_eyebrow`, `app_hero_eyebrow`, `ai_hero_eyebrow` were registered but rendered by nothing (all empty in the DB). Removed with notes. If a design ever gains a hero eyebrow on those pages, copy the ES hero field + markup rather than re-adding a dead field.

### MCS card artwork — source of truth
Cards take their photo from the **stored `mcs_cards` ACF rows**, not the template default array, so every image change needs a media import + `mcs_cards_<i>_image` update on Local *and* Dev. Current row order: 0 Column Risers, 1 Safety & Environmental, 2 Sheet Metal, 3 Auto Doors (video, row also has a `video` sub-field), 4 Hydraulic–Pneumatics, 5 Custom Workholding, 6 Process Engineering, 7 Specialty Machine.

**`custom-fixtures.jpg` and `custom-workholding.jpg` are deliberately different photos** — the former is now only the gallery collection "Custom Fixture Design" cover/lightbox, the latter is the service card. Don't collapse them.

### Portrait artwork in landscape cards
The MCS cards are 275px tall and landscape (~2.15), so `object-fit: cover` shows only a **~26% centred vertical band** of a portrait source. Preview the crop before assuming it works — `sips -c <h> <w>` reproduces it exactly (e.g. `sips -c 472 1012` for a 1012-wide asset).

### STANDING RULE — ACF fields must be APPLIED, not just defined
Registering a field only makes the **front end** render its template default; the **editor** still shows an empty control. Nothing looks broken, which is why this gets missed. After any ACF add/rename/change:

1. Field definition **+ template default** (defaults live in the template, never `default_value`).
2. Add it to `scripts/seed-acf-content.php` — using the **field key**, not the name.
3. `./scripts/sync-theme-to-local.sh` → seed → audit.
4. Deploy the theme to Dev **and run the seeder there** — a theme push does NOT apply fields.
5. Confirm with `scripts/audit-acf-applied.php`.

**Blanks that are correct — never "fix" these:** all `*_hero_accent_color` / `*_hero_cta_color` (blank = keep the design colour), `es_show_news` (blank = hidden), `es_partners_logos` (wordmark fallback is the design), `haas_brand_logo` / `cta_image` (theme-bundled), `mcs_cta_body` / `app_cta_body` (deliberately empty).

**Traps already caught (read before touching ACF or media):**

1. **Never compare bare slugs — the site is hierarchical.** `rotary-repair` (#1484 → `/rotary-repair/`) and `service/rotary-repair` (#194 → `/service/rotary-repair/`) are **two different pages, both live, both 200**. Comparing slugs made #194 look like an unreachable duplicate and nearly got a live URL trashed. Compare full paths with `get_page_uri()`. **Nothing was deleted.**
2. **Locate field groups by `page_template`, not `post_name`, when a slug is not unique.** `group_rotary_content` used `post_name == 'rotary-repair'` and so appeared on `/service/rotary-repair/` — a page running `page-service.php` that never reads those nine fields. Editors saw controls that did nothing.
3. **`media_handle_sideload()` MOVES the file it is given.** Importing a theme asset into the media library with it will `rename()` the asset out of the theme — the import appears to succeed while the source quietly disappears. Stage a `wp_tempnam()` copy first (`scripts/set-card-image.php` shows the pattern). The tell is that `sync-theme-to-local.sh` then reports "0 files updated".
4. **`sips --cropOffset` silently fails on WebP input** (no output file, no error). Convert to JPEG first, then crop. Also note `--cropOffset 0 0` is treated as *unset* and falls back to a centred crop — use `1 0` when you actually want a top-anchored crop.
5. `update_field()` with a field **name** instead of a **key** silently writes junk meta (`field_cta_call_label`) that nothing reads, while still reporting success — if a seed says "set" but the audit disagrees, check the key.

**The 2017-era Service sub-pages are LIVE:** `submit-a-request`, `parts-order`, `rotary-repair`, `preventive-maintenance-plan`, `application-support` all still resolve under `/service/…` and run `page-service.php`. Do not delete them without asking the client.

### Applications gallery collections
`app_collections` holds a `media` textarea, one pipe-delimited item per line (`type | src | poster | alt | caption`). The per-collection `meta` is a **static label describing the whole set** — the "N photos" badge is computed separately by `gallery-module.js`. Adding images needs the stored rows updated (a stored value beats the template default): `wp eval-file scripts/add-app-gallery-items.php "<collection title>" ["meta=..."] "src|alt|caption" ...` (positional args, idempotent by filename).

### Page-level images (hero, CTA band)
Same trap as cards: the live image is usually a media-library **attachment**, so changing `assets/images/<file>` only changes the default. Use `wp eval-file scripts/set-page-image.php "<page slug>" "<image field>" "assets/images/<file>.jpg"` (positional args, idempotent). **Run it only for the field you actually mean to change** — the ES and Automation CTA bands share one photo, and pointing the script at both re-imported a lower-resolution copy over the ES band's 2560px upload, which had to be reverted.

### Card images — two halves
On the rebuilt pages the **cards** store media-library attachments (in a repeater such as `ai_cards` / `app_cards`) while **galleries** use theme-relative paths. Replacing `assets/images/<file>` updates the gallery/default but leaves the card on its old upload, so a DB step is always needed: `wp eval-file scripts/set-card-image.php "<page slug>" "<repeater field>" "<card title>" "assets/images/<file>.jpg"` (positional args — WP-CLI rejects custom `--flags` on `eval-file`). Idempotent.

### Figma access from this session
No Figma MCP is available here, but `~/.figma_token` exists — use the REST API directly: `/v1/files/:key/nodes?ids=<a:b>` to identify a node, read an IMAGE fill's `imageRef`, then `/v1/files/:key/images` to resolve the original. `/v1/images/:key?ids=…&format=png&scale=2` renders any node to a PNG for visual checking. File key `YgHwqyyFj57c1ZSbmfkL0c`.

### MCS service cards — `mcs_cards` repeater
The card grid is an ACF repeater (`title`, `image`, `video` (optional), `detail`). **The stored rows override the template's default array** — `$cards = $pick( 'mcs_cards', <default> )` — so adding a key to the PHP default changes nothing on Local/Dev until the row is seeded. `video` makes a card a muted inline looping thumbnail (`autoplay muted loop playsinline`, `image` as poster, `aria-hidden`); `animations.js` pauses it under `prefers-reduced-motion`. Only Auto Doors uses it so far; `auto-door.mp4` is 4.4MB and downloads with the page.

