### Homepage hero colour selects — no ACF defaults (2026-09-22, commit `94332cd`)
`accent_color` / `cta_color` deliberately have **no `default_value`** (`''` + `allow_null` + `placeholder`). ACF **injects a field's `default_value` on read** when a repeater row has no stored value, so a default would silently override the positional design colours (slide 1 Haas red, rest Brand Orange) on any database that predates the field — and a naive wp-admin "Update" would then persist that wrong value. Blank now means "no explicit choice" and falls through to the retired `accent_class` meta, then to the design default. Same blank-default pattern is used by every interior `*_hero_accent_color` / `*_hero_cta_color` field. Re-seed with `scripts/seed-home-hero-colors.php` (idempotent; `wp eval-file`, needs to be copied to the server since `scripts/` is not part of a theme-only push).

