- **⚠️ ACF injects `default_value` on read — now neutralised (2026-09-21, opencode).** A repeater row with no stored value returns the field default, *not* empty — so a field with a default silently changes the design the moment anyone saves. Worse, this **actually fired on Local during DSH testing**: opening Home in the editor (fields showed the old `white`/`orange` defaults) and clicking Update persisted `white` over all six fields, wiping slide 1's Haas red. Fixed properly rather than guarded: both selects now have **no default_value and `allow_null`**, so the editor shows blank ("Leave unset to keep the design colour") and a save persists nothing. `front-page.php` resolves blank → (1) retired `accent_class` meta read **raw** with `get_post_meta()` (it is unregistered, so absent from the ACF row), then (2) the **design treatment (slide 1 Haas red, rest orange)** — matching `scripts/seed-home-hero-colors.php`. Seeds are idempotent. A fresh env (Dev) renders the design correctly with no DB work.
