HOST="gerotechdev@gerotechdev.ssh.wpengine.net"
NAS="/nas/content/live/gerotechdev"

# 1. theme (rsync over ssh works; scp/sftp does NOT — "subsystem request failed")
rsync -avz --delete -e "ssh -i \"$KEY\" -o BatchMode=yes -o ServerAliveInterval=10" wp-content/themes/gerotech-child/ "$HOST:$NAS/wp-content/themes/gerotech-child/"

# 2. seed colours: WPE's ~/home is EPHEMERAL per-container (a file written via
#    one ssh dies on the next), so don't scp scripts — pipe stdin:
ssh -i "$KEY" "$HOST" "cd $NAS && wp eval-file -" < /path/to/seed.php

# 3. hero art: media_handle_sideload the pushed theme asset, set the field
#    (see dev-hero-import.php style — also works for ES). Then:
ssh -i "$KEY" "$HOST" "cd $NAS && wp page-cache flush && wp cdn-cache flush"
```
Gotchas: `wp eval-file -` reads PHP from stdin (boots WP, so theme helpers like `gerotech_image_srcset()` exist). `~` for a *short-command* ssh also resolves `/home/wpe-user` (ephemeral) — always use stdin or `$NAS` paths. `wp` emits harmless parent-theme `$feature` notices at CLI — ignore (source: gerotech `functions.php`, not child). Page slugs (AS of 09-18): ES `engineered-solutions`, MCS `modification-of-standard-machine-tools`, Apps `unique-applications-for-standard-machines`, Automation `automated-system` (not the goose-chase slugs `machine-custom-solutions` / `automation-integration` → 404).

**`scripts/seed-home-hero-colors.php`** (repo, committed) is idempotent and safe on any environment: stored choice wins → retired `accent_class` meta → original treatment. Verified by simulating a theme-only deploy on Local.

