### 2026-09-16 session (opencode — gallery module: collections + video)
- **Client request:** current flat one-photo-per-card gallery is wrong — they want **multiple images per category + a video option**. Built as an **isolated preview module** to share with the PM before rolling out to pages.
- **New (untracked, nothing on live pages touched):**
  - `gallery-module-preview.html` — exploratory preview page. Content mirrors MCS (7 categories from the current 13 flat cards). Header/footer partials + scripts included. Carries a "Preview module — not linked in the site nav" note.
  - `assets/css/gallery-module.css` — namespaced `.gallery-collection*` + `.gallery-viewer*`. Deliberately **self-contained** (does not reuse/override `.mcs-gallery-*` / `.gallery-lightbox`). Responsive ladder 4→3→2→1.
  - `assets/js/gallery-module.js` — parses `<template class="gallery-collection__data">` per card; derives count badges + `--has-video` class; builds a viewer scoped to the opened collection; supports images **and** `<video controls playsinline>`; keyboard (Esc/←/→/Tab trap), swipe, focus restore.
  - `assets/videos/placeholder-*.mp4` — ffmpeg-generated sample clips, clearly commented as placeholders awaiting client footage.
- **Data model:** each `.gallery-collection` card = one category; a `<template>` child lists its media as `[data-type="image|video"][data-src][data-poster][data-alt][data-caption]`. Badges/counts are derived, so authors only edit markup (maps cleanly to a WP ACF repeater later).
- **Card a11y:** heading holds a real `<button class="gallery-collection__trigger">`; `::after` stretches it over the card (valid HTML — no block content inside a button).
- **Verified:** chrome-headless-shell screenshots at 1440 + 390; image viewer (title/caption/`2 / 4`/active thumb), video viewer (poster + native controls + play badge on thumb), mobile 1-col. Live pages untouched.
- **Not done / next:** PM review → on approval promote module and convert MCS (13 cards → 7 collections), then Automation + Applications. No `href`/nav entry added anywhere.

